repository-code: "https://github.com/tranducle/RAISR-SME"
url: "https://raisr-sme.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of the RAISR-SME v1.0 25-item ternary cyber-AI
  self-assessment instrument and the deterministic two-arm empirical and Monte
  Carlo replication suite for ICIIT 2027. Includes the frozen item bank
  (bank_v1.json), authoritative NIST CSF 2.0 subcategory crosswalk and verifier
  (verify_ids.py), three bit-exact scoring engines (Python stdlib, browser
  JavaScript, and NumPy), automated parity tests across 20,006 vectors, and
  four analysis suites (exp1 to exp4) evaluating UK Cyber Security Breaches
  Survey (2023 to 2025) skip-routing and size strata, UK Cyber Security
  Longitudinal Survey (Waves 1 to 4) Mundlak and timing models, and 50,000
  empirically anchored Monte Carlo SME profiles. Licensed UK Data Archive
  microdata is withheld per End User Licence and documented with SHA-256
  checksums and access instructions in data/README.md.
keywords:
  - SME cybersecurity
  - generative AI governance
  - formative index validation
  - epistemic uncertainty
  - reporting bias
  - longitudinal panel data
license: MIT
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
